<title>JAPAN: Japan trade minister says yen weakness troublesome.</title>
<headline>Japan trade minister says yen weakness troublesome.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade Minister Shinji Sato said on Tuesday that an excessively weak yen was troublesome for Japan's economy.</p>
<p>Asked about the yen's recent weakness against the dollar, Sato told reporters: &quot;A too weak yen is troublesome, as Japan buys raw materials, manufactures and exports products. There is both an import and export side, so it's a difficult problem.&quot;</p>
<p>The dollar hit a 46-month high of 117.00 yen on Monday but dipped below 115 yen at Tuesday noon.</p>
</text>
